Changelog: 21-10-2026 20:24:57

Release 0.7.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 18:34:48

Added. The suite's own patch for the driver (mesa/bc250-suite-mesa-26.2.1.patch), applied on top of DirectMesh's: a
new switch, Split mesh shaders that write memory (RADV_BC250_MESH_SPLIT_WRITES=1), lets the driver split large mesh
shaders that store to buffers, or use an atomic's result to decide such stores, as the fault reporting of PS5
emulators does (SILENT HILL stopped at "BC250 mesh split rejected"). Those writes run once, in the first piece of the
split. It is off unless chosen per game, because the driver cannot check that the game never reads the writes back.
The build applies the patch and names it ("suite patch" and the start of its SHA-256); a build from before it shows
as outdated, so build, install and test again.

