Release 0.2.1.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:32:49

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/mesh (was apps/mesh-shaders) and its package is mesh_shaders (was
bc250_mesh_shaders): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package named
after the app without the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the portal, its
chapter of the wiki (apps/mesh/, which the Manual link opens), its installer test and its release tags:
mesh-v<x.y.z> from the next release on, which the app's update check follows. The installed app keeps its name,
its launcher bc250-mesh-shaders, its folder under /opt, the script, the build, the test results, the driver in
/usr/local/lib/bc250-mesh-shaders and the launch options wrapper, so the launch options set in Steam stay as they
are. The portal moves its record of the installed copy to the new key.

